      "decision": "retainNote",
      "finding": "The complete het has a broad lower bar almost reaching its left leg, joined to the right leg and continuing into a low right-hand terminal. Literal het-patah in מִפָּחַד and וַיְחַבֶּק supplies a detached transverse bar; local רוּחָהּ supplies a distinct qamats head-and-stem. The target resembles a joined qamats but its right terminal is continuous with the letter leg and does not independently identify the point. Joined or distorted lower marks remain a live competitor; no vowel is certified.",
