      "decision": "retainNote",
      "finding": "The complete zayin narrows below its head and ends in a shallow, broad basal bar with slight underside irregularities. Literal qamats in זָהָב/הַזָּהָב has a clear downward stem; literal sheva in בִּזְרוֹעוֹתָיו has a two-level extension. Local לֵב shows a joined horizontal tsere pair, while בְּזַעַם demonstrates a vowel bar joined to the same letter stem. The target gives no unique pair, stem or separate point shape, so its vowel remains unreadable.",
